    <item>
      <title>From: B.H., To: Ruby Chandler</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1908/08/13/186/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 1908 22:43:46 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1908/08/13/186/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_16441248_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140414_16441248_0001&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_16441248_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_16442035_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140414_16442035_0002&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_16442035_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;  &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: B.H., To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Postcard Info: The Pen-Art Publishing CO., Bloomington, Illinois&lt;br&gt;
Mailed from: Normal, Illinois on August 13, 1908&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Looked for a card here now but it came OK. Hope you enjoyed your visit. Did the “one” you met look good to you? I will be home midnight August 26. Wish I could com eon the moon train but can’t. I have thought of you often since you journeyed up here.&lt;br&gt;
Yours as B.H.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
